# lazyit — Zitadel IdP site block (ADR-0037, ADR-0086). See infra/caddy/Caddyfile.
#
# This file is imported by the main Caddyfile via `import sites/*.caddy`, but it is only PRESENT in
# the Caddy container when the bundled Zitadel IdP is opted in: infra/docker-compose.oidc.yaml mounts
# it at /etc/caddy/sites/auth.caddy. In local-auth mode (AUTH_MODE=local, the default) and in BYOI the
# oidc overlay is not loaded, so this file is absent, the glob matches nothing, and Caddy neither
# serves auth.{domain} nor requests an (unusable) certificate for it. It reuses the (security_headers)
# and (access_log) snippets defined in the main Caddyfile (import is textual, resolved before parse).
#
# Zitadel runs on the internal Docker network without its own TLS (--tlsMode external; Caddy terminates
# HTTPS here and proxies to Zitadel's internal HTTP listener). Set LAZYIT_DOMAIN to your base domain
# (e.g. "lazyit.example.com") in .env.prod; local prod-like uses "localhost" (Caddy's internal CA).
auth.{$LAZYIT_DOMAIN:localhost} {
	import security_headers
	import access_log
	reverse_proxy zitadel:8080
}
